---
import '../styles/custom.css';
import '../styles/index-page.css';
import AgentMeta from '../components/AgentMeta.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import ThemeProvider from '../components/ThemeProvider.astro';
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Verify receipt · Froglet</title>
<meta name="description" content="Verify Froglet signatures, canonical hashes, and artifact chains locally in your browser." />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://froglet.dev/verify-receipt/" />
<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Froglet" />
<meta property="og:title" content="Verify receipt · Froglet" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Verify Froglet signatures, canonical hashes, and artifact chains locally in your browser." />
<meta property="og:url" content="https://froglet.dev/verify-receipt/" />
<meta property="og:image" content="https://froglet.dev/og/default.png" />
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="Verify receipt · Froglet" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Verify Froglet signatures, canonical hashes, and artifact chains locally in your browser." />
<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://froglet.dev/og/default.png" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
<AgentMeta route="verifyReceipt" />
<ThemeProvider />
</head>
<body data-screen-label="Receipt verifier">
<SiteHeader currentPath={Astro.url.pathname} />
<main class="froglet-home-main verify-page" data-agent-task="receipt-artifact-verify">
  <section class="hero verify-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Receipt verifier</span>
    <h1>See what a signed receipt can prove.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Check a sample, then see what happens when a receipt is changed.
      No account, installation, or payment. Your pasted data stays in this browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-demo" aria-label="Try verification">
    <div class="verify-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn primary" data-receipt-sample>Verify sample chain</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn ghost" data-receipt-tamper>Check tampered sample</button>
    </div>
    <p class="verify-hint">These buttons load public example records, not a live transaction. They replace the JSON below. The tampered sample changes one receipt field without signing it again.</p>
    <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to run the verifier locally in your browser.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-grid verify-grid--guided" aria-label="Local artifact verifier">
    <article class="verify-panel verify-panel--result">
      <div class="verify-panel-head"><h2>Verification result</h2></div>
      <div class="verify-output" data-receipt-output tabindex="-1" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
        <p>Start with <strong>Verify sample chain</strong>. You should see five signed records pass verification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="verify-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn ghost" data-receipt-copy disabled>Copy report</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn ghost" data-receipt-download disabled>Download report</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn ghost" data-receipt-clear>Clear</button>
      </div>
      <p class="verify-hint" data-receipt-export-status role="status"></p>
      <details class="verify-raw-report" data-receipt-export hidden>
        <summary>Report text — select and copy</summary>
        <textarea data-receipt-export-text readonly aria-label="Verification report JSON"></textarea>
      </details>
    </article>

    <details class="verify-panel verify-editor" data-receipt-editor>
      <summary>Inspect the sample or verify your own JSON</summary>
      <p class="verify-hint" id="receipt-input-help">Paste one signed artifact, an array of artifacts, or an object with an <code>artifacts</code> array. Include the full chain to check the agreement and receipt together.</p>
      <textarea
        class="verify-input"
        data-receipt-input
        spellcheck="false"
        autocomplete="off"
        aria-label="Receipt or artifact envelope JSON"
        aria-describedby="receipt-input-help"
        placeholder='{"artifacts": [{"artifact_type": "receipt", ...}]}'
      ></textarea>
      <div class="verify-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn primary" data-receipt-verify>Verify evidence</button>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="verify-next" aria-label="Next steps">
    <h2>Use it with your agent</h2>
    <p>The sample shows that a changed record fails verification. The <a href="/learn/cloud-trial/">hosted demo</a> is temporarily unavailable while its origin is moved. To create a fresh result with your own service, <a href="/learn/quickstart/">prepare a local setup</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block verify-boundary">
    <span class="eyebrow">Verification boundary</span>
    <h2>What this page can and cannot prove.</h2>
    <div class="entry-grid">
      <div class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">01 · checked locally</div>
        <h3>Signatures and chain links</h3>
        <p>This page verifies BIP340/Schnorr signatures, canonical hashes, artifact rules, and links between supplied records. The Rust verifier runs as WebAssembly. Missing or duplicate chain members are reported explicitly. A valid signature alone is not a complete chain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="entry-card">
        <div class="entry-num">02 · limits</div>
        <h3>Evidence is not a guarantee of truth</h3>
        <p>Signatures identify keys. They do not prove a human or organization authorized the action, that an output is correct, or that a payment settled externally. Historical verification does not check expiration against today's clock. This sample is a conformance fixture, not a live customer transaction.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter />
</main>

<script>
import { initReceiptVerifier } from '../scripts/receipt-verifier';
initReceiptVerifier();
</script>
<style>
.verify-output pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.8rem; }
.verify-output { color: var(--fg1); scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
.verify-hero { padding-bottom: 2rem; }
</style>
</body>
</html>
